4.Subject to the provisions of this Act and any otherwritten law, the Foundation shall have the power:–

(a) to request and recive contributions, grants, donationsand gifts of all forms as may be necessary for thepurpose of the Foundation;

(b) to purchase, rent, lease or otherwise obtain lands orbuildings which may be required for the purpose ofthe Foundation;

(c) to borrow or raise funds with or without interest forthe purposes of the Foundaion;

(d) to make, draw, accept, discount, endorse, buy, selland issue bills of exchange, cheques, promissorynotes and other negotiable instruments and to open,operate, maintain, and close accounts in anybank;

(e) to invest any funds not immediately required forthe purposes of the Foundation, in such manner asthe Executive Council may deem necessary;

(f) to enter into agreement or contracts with any personor any company or body of persons with a view topromoting the objects of the Foundation;

